{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["The sense of <b>בימים ההם</b> is after saying 'in the days of Ahasuerus' at the beginning of the matters, for the first is a general statement. And the sense of 'when the king Ahasuerus sat' — that he rested from the wars of India and Cush, for he was mighty, and thus it is written in the scroll: 'therefore in the third year of his reign.'" "<b>שושן הבירה.</b> The name of a palace, as in 'for not to man [is it,] the birah.' And this palace was within the province of Elam, as written in the book of Daniel. And as you find in this scroll, Shushan is the name of a province near Elam, and most of the province [consists of] Israel, as I shall explain. Many said that he made a feast because he calculated according to his reckoning and saw that Israel would not be redeemed. And some say [he made it] because he rested from wars. And some say [because] he married Vashti — and this is the correct one in my eyes."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites 'therefore in the third year of his reign' as written במגלה, by which he apparently means the verse of Esther itself (1:3), not an external source; 'במגלה' read literally as 'in the scroll [of Esther].'"}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:41.181509348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}